## Summary

This is the `spring-petclinic-rest` app. Owner creation happens in the **V1 controller** (`addOwner`), which already implements exactly the 409-conflict pattern you want to extend. Notably, **there is already a failing acceptance test** (`AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateEmail`) expecting duplicate-email creation to return 409 — the feature itself is not yet implemented.

---

### 1. Owner entity
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`

`@Entity @Table(name = "owners")`, extends `Person` (which supplies `firstName`/`lastName`). The email field is minimally mapped (no uniqueness/validation constraint):
```java
@Column(name = "email")
private String email;

public String getEmail() { return this.email; }
public void setEmail(String email) { this.email = email; }
```
There is no `deleted`/soft-delete column on the entity despite a test-helper comment implying one (see note at the end).

### 2. Repository
Interface: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`

The directly relevant convention is the telephone existence check (mirror this for email):
```java
